WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.302
In real projects, we usually do not type records manually.

00:00:04.302 --> 00:00:12.587
Data often comes from a CSV file, an exported report, an API, or a database query.

00:00:12.587 --> 00:00:20.182
Pandas provides the read CSV function to load comma-separated data directly into a DataFrame.

00:00:20.182 --> 00:00:30.042
This example uses string I O so everything can run inside the browser, but conceptually it behaves like reading a small

00:00:30.042 --> 00:00:35.675
file from disk. After loading the data, we print the table and check its Python type.

00:00:36.297 --> 00:00:42.944
A common professional workflow is to use SQL to retrieve the necessary records from a database,

00:00:42.944 --> 00:00:49.296
then use Pandas for additional inspection, cleaning, transformation, and analysis.
